// Message catalogue for the sentences the packages produce: code -> {en, de}. A package result carries the
// English sentence and, next to it, its code and named parameters (aqt_evidence.Text); the page shows the
// German from here with the parameters filled into {name} and falls back to the English text the package
// sent. "en" is exactly the package's template (tests/test_messages.py checks it), so a stored sentence
// without a code can also be matched against "en". A parameter can itself be {code, args}; the code
// "aqt.join" joins its args.items with args.sep. Evidence content (reasons, notes, names, ids) is a
// parameter and is never translated. One entry per line; this file is JSON between the braces.

